   "source": [
    "# Expense Classifier ML\n",
    "### Predicting Account Names from Expense Line Items\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Executive Summary\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook builds a machine learning pipeline to automatically classify expense line items\n",
    "into their correct accounting categories. The primary signal comes from free-text fields\n",
    "(`itemName` / `itemDescription`) combined with vendor identity and transaction amount features.\n",
    "We tackle **103 target classes** across **4,894 records**, with severe class imbalance\n",
    "(the dominant class holds 1,179 samples while 16 classes have only 1 sample each).\n",
    "\n",
    "**Strategy:**\n",
    "- TF-IDF on item text (word n-grams + character n-grams) as the primary signal\n",
    "- Vendor one-hot encoding — many vendors always bill to the same account\n",
    "- Log-transformed amount + amount bucket as auxiliary numeric features\n",
    "- Linear SVC + Logistic Regression evaluated; best selected automatically\n",
    "- 5-fold stratified cross-validation for robust accuracy estimates\n",
    "\n",
    "**Notebook layout:**\n",
    "1. Environment Setup\n",
    "2. Data Loading and Validation\n",
    "3. Exploratory Data Analysis\n",
    "4. Feature Engineering\n",
    "5. Model Training and Selection\n",
    "6. Final Evaluation and Results\n",
    "7. Discussion\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 1. Environment Setup\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
